1
00:00:53,180 --> 00:00:57,710
Therefore, the defense's request,
a medical demonstration is denied,

2
00:00:57,850 --> 00:01:00,620
and the defendant is sentenced
to the maximum penalty allowed by law,

3
00:01:01,080 --> 00:01:02,820
the death penalty.

4
00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:12,800
(Defendant)

5
00:01:29,810 --> 00:01:30,810
Excuse me, Your Honor.

6
00:01:35,020 --> 00:01:38,860
Why did you give more weight
to the Forensic Service's findings?

7
00:01:38,990 --> 00:01:40,920
Because I had to err
on the side of caution.

8
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:43,630
But that completely rules out
its potential as a treatment.

9
00:01:43,690 --> 00:01:48,330
What's important in this case
is the murder, not the treatment.

10
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:52,170
Considering the potential benefits
for patients with incurable diseases,

11
00:01:52,340 --> 00:01:54,240
shouldn't you at least allow
the medical demonstration?

12
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:57,510
The court believes that
being protected from crime...

13
00:01:57,570 --> 00:02:00,110
is a greater public interest
than receiving treatment.

14
00:02:00,180 --> 00:02:03,110
Terminally ill children are also
desperately waiting for that treatment.

15
00:02:03,180 --> 00:02:06,450
- If we turn our back on that hope...
- Counsel!

16
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:22,270
- Here she comes!
- Here she comes!

17
00:02:23,770 --> 00:02:25,170
A motive has been established.

18
00:02:25,230 --> 00:02:28,370
Why did you insist it was a random killing
in the early stages of the investigation?

19
00:02:28,470 --> 00:02:31,310
The case is still ongoing,
so I can't comment at this time.

20
00:02:33,380 --> 00:02:34,940
- One more comment, please!
- What's next for the trial?

21
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:40,280
(Prosecutor Cha Yi Yeon)

22
00:02:41,450 --> 00:02:43,750
- Prosecutor Cha?
- She isn't in yet.

23
00:02:44,790 --> 00:02:47,460
She said she went to another crime scene
and would be back late.

24
00:02:57,570 --> 00:02:59,540
- Yes, Director Oh.
- Where are you right now?

25
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:01,000
I'm working.

26
00:03:01,570 --> 00:03:03,610
I told you to be
at the Criminal Division Meeting.

27
00:03:03,710 --> 00:03:06,010
Everyone came for you. What's the point
if the guest of honor isn't here?

28
00:03:06,910 --> 00:03:09,510
The first trial just ended.
This is no time to celebrate.

29
00:03:09,580 --> 00:03:12,150
There you go again.
This is why you never get ahead.

30
00:03:14,650 --> 00:03:17,220
- The trial comes first, Director.
- Spare me.

31
00:03:17,950 --> 00:03:20,190
At least drop by the team dinner later.
All right?

32
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:22,860
I'll see how things are
and get back to you.

33
00:03:28,630 --> 00:03:29,630
Ligature marks?

34
00:03:29,930 --> 00:03:33,140
- It definitely looks like a homicide.
- The murder weapon?

35
00:03:33,670 --> 00:03:37,740
Nothing was found at the scene,
but we'll need to investigate further.

36
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:41,840
It could be someone connected
to Lee Woo Gyeom.

37
00:03:42,210 --> 00:03:45,210
Right, we'll look into that too
and get back to you.

38
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:50,890
Yes. Hello? Right.

39
00:03:51,420 --> 00:03:52,420
Okay.

40
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:00,800
(Jinnam Medical Research Institute)

41
00:04:03,300 --> 00:04:05,600
(Jinnam Medical Research Institute)

42
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:12,440
(One Last Chance)

43
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:14,410
(Lee Woo Gyeom Sentenced to Death,
Defense Appeals)

44
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:15,580
(Results of Lee Woo Gyeom's 1st Trial)

45
00:04:15,650 --> 00:04:16,680
(Med Demo Denied, Death Sentence Issued)

46
00:04:16,750 --> 00:04:17,750
(Lee Woo Gyeom: Defense Appeals)

47
00:04:21,250 --> 00:04:23,290
(Killer Lee Woo Gyeom Sentenced to Death,
Defense Immediately Appeals)

48
00:04:24,450 --> 00:04:26,890
I see Judge Choi is presiding
over the appeal.

49
00:04:27,890 --> 00:04:29,060
Perfect setup, isn't it?

50
00:04:29,960 --> 00:04:32,830
So you can ride the momentum
and absolutely crush that jerk, Park,

51
00:04:33,500 --> 00:04:35,530
I had him assigned.
We were classmates at the institute.

52
00:04:36,730 --> 00:04:40,700
Don't you think Attorney Park has
another card up his sleeve for the appeal?

53
00:04:41,470 --> 00:04:43,440
In golf, the most important thing
is the address.

54
00:04:43,710 --> 00:04:46,310
Your initial stance.
If your stance is off,

55
00:04:46,880 --> 00:04:50,680
even Tiger Woods will shank it.
But Park Han Jun?

56
00:04:51,250 --> 00:04:53,380
His swing is based on
a fundamentally flawed stance.

57
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:55,920
He can try a million times,
but it's no use.

58
00:04:58,320 --> 00:05:01,520
Besides, the first trial set a precedent
for the appellate court.

59
00:05:02,090 --> 00:05:04,090
The public's interest isn't
in receiving treatment.

60
00:05:04,790 --> 00:05:06,100
It's being protected.

61
00:05:07,060 --> 00:05:08,200
Yes, that's right.

62
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:15,240
(Poll: For or Against,
Lee Woo Gyeom's Medical Demo)

63
00:05:15,300 --> 00:05:16,340
What is this?

64
00:05:17,510 --> 00:05:19,340
Chief Bang, take a look at this.

65
00:05:21,840 --> 00:05:26,680
"Fun to watch a murderer's medical demo?
Let's take a poll."

66
00:05:26,850 --> 00:05:29,420
Posts like these keep popping up nonstop.

67
00:05:30,520 --> 00:05:31,520
Click to see the results.

68
00:05:32,120 --> 00:05:33,120
Okay.

69
00:05:33,290 --> 00:05:34,290
(Results)

70
00:05:35,390 --> 00:05:37,490
Seventy-five percent? Are you serious?

71
00:05:38,030 --> 00:05:41,200
- Seriously, why would people...
- What's so funny?

72
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:49,310
The medical demo memes are going viral,
and the response is insane.

73
00:05:50,210 --> 00:05:52,840
People online will make a joke
out of anything.

74
00:05:53,640 --> 00:05:56,950
Still, we can't ignore it.
This can easily shape public opinion.

75
00:05:57,780 --> 00:06:00,220
- Are there a lot of posts like that?
- Yes.

76
00:06:00,980 --> 00:06:02,220
Just look at this.

77
00:06:04,290 --> 00:06:05,290
(He wants to avoid the death sentence)

78
00:06:05,350 --> 00:06:06,490
(He's our ticket to leading in medicine)

79
00:06:06,560 --> 00:06:08,090
(So will our country get rich?
He's my cousin's only hope)

80
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:09,160
(No one else dies. So why not try it?)

81
00:06:12,530 --> 00:06:14,000
What's the public sentiment
like out there?

82
00:06:14,900 --> 00:06:16,430
It should have shifted in my favor by now.

83
00:06:17,670 --> 00:06:20,970
So you care more about public opinion
than the trial's outcome?

84
00:06:22,140 --> 00:06:26,340
We already expected this verdict.
Death penalty cases go to a third trial,

85
00:06:26,540 --> 00:06:29,010
so we need to win over
as many people as possible by then.

86
00:06:31,150 --> 00:06:34,980
As a matter of fact,
regardless of the verdict,

87
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:38,790
there's growing talk that your ability
to cure people should be tested.

88
00:06:38,950 --> 00:06:42,090
Your blood mutation was
officially recognized in the States.

89
00:06:42,830 --> 00:06:45,460
So we're going to appeal
and ask the court...

90
00:06:45,530 --> 00:06:48,560
to re-evaluate the value
of your treatment.

91
00:06:49,170 --> 00:06:50,170
And...

92
00:06:51,570 --> 00:06:53,170
we're also going to request
what you want most.

93
00:06:53,570 --> 00:06:55,570
The medical demonstration.

94
00:06:57,140 --> 00:06:58,140
Good.

95
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:00,640
However, I'm afraid...

96
00:07:01,740 --> 00:07:03,050
that the medical demonstration...

97
00:07:03,810 --> 00:07:05,680
is very likely to be rejected.

98
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:10,350
The appeals judge is an old classmate
of Director Oh, Prosecutor Cha's boss.

99
00:07:17,930 --> 00:07:19,200
Come on, so what?

100
00:07:20,660 --> 00:07:22,500
If I can't do the medical demonstration,

101
00:07:22,900 --> 00:07:25,030
then there's no point
in having this trial.

102
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:27,470
Lee Woo Gyeom.

103
00:07:31,670 --> 00:07:33,340
We need to have a backup plan.

104
00:07:44,890 --> 00:07:46,160
Gosh.

105
00:07:59,340 --> 00:08:00,740
(Wife)

106
00:08:01,470 --> 00:08:02,770
I'm putting Min Seo on.

107
00:08:03,070 --> 00:08:05,040
- Okay.
- Daddy.

108
00:08:11,250 --> 00:08:15,050
Hi, sweetie. What are you still doing up?

109
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:17,020
You must miss Daddy a lot, huh?

110
00:08:17,420 --> 00:08:18,590
I do, Daddy.

111
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:21,390
When are you coming home?

112
00:08:23,460 --> 00:08:27,600
If my sweet Min Seo says she misses me,
I'd come running there right this second.

113
00:08:28,160 --> 00:08:32,740
Really? Mom, Daddy says he can come!

114
00:08:33,070 --> 00:08:36,940
You've seen Daddy, so it's time for bed.
Let's talk with Daddy later.

115
00:08:40,240 --> 00:08:41,580
Daddy...

116
00:08:42,140 --> 00:08:44,280
Mommy says I have to go to bed now.

117
00:08:45,610 --> 00:08:47,320
Okay, sweetheart...

118
00:08:48,120 --> 00:08:51,350
It's really late now,
so I think that's a good idea.

119
00:08:51,720 --> 00:08:54,720
You missed me a lot too, right?

120
00:08:56,790 --> 00:08:57,890
Daddy...

121
00:08:58,660 --> 00:08:59,660
always...

122
00:09:00,460 --> 00:09:03,130
Every single day,
he misses his little girl.

123
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:05,900
Daddy needs to get to sleep too.
Come on, say good night.

124
00:09:07,840 --> 00:09:12,310
- I'm going to bed, Daddy. Sweet dreams.
- Okay.

125
00:09:13,710 --> 00:09:14,780
You too, sweetie.

126
00:09:16,780 --> 00:09:18,050
Have sweet dreams.

127
00:09:48,640 --> 00:09:50,680
Human trial results.

128
00:09:51,710 --> 00:09:52,820
Batten disease.

129
00:09:53,880 --> 00:09:54,880
Counselor.

130
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:58,020
Batten disease is incurable.

131
00:09:58,890 --> 00:10:01,960
Especially for someone like Min Seo,
once the initial symptoms appear,

132
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:05,190
death within a few years is a certainty.

133
00:10:05,900 --> 00:10:06,960
Can you really...

134
00:10:08,100 --> 00:10:09,870
cure Batten disease?

135
00:10:10,470 --> 00:10:11,530
Let's just say that...

136
00:10:12,840 --> 00:10:14,540
I can cure Min Seo.

137
00:10:32,490 --> 00:10:35,120
Prosecutor, I ran a background check
on the deceased.

138
00:10:35,490 --> 00:10:40,330
- He's Song Min Su. He worked at JNI.
- The research institute?

139
00:10:41,430 --> 00:10:42,530
(Report: Song Min Su and Jinnam Institute)

140
00:10:43,230 --> 00:10:45,200
(Victim Identification Report)

141
00:10:45,270 --> 00:10:47,070
And I'm not sure if this is a coincidence.

142
00:10:47,700 --> 00:10:51,110
You remember the evidence
that Attorney Park submitted, right?

143
00:10:51,740 --> 00:10:53,940
The files on that treatment
Lee Woo Gyeom researched...

144
00:10:54,540 --> 00:10:56,450
back when he was a med student.

145
00:10:57,450 --> 00:11:01,650
This is the research for a treatment
the defendant submitted...

146
00:11:01,920 --> 00:11:03,920
to a competition held by
the global medical group, Chaeum.

147
00:11:04,250 --> 00:11:08,560
At the time, the defendant's idea
was highly praised by Chaeum's team,

148
00:11:08,620 --> 00:11:12,760
and we've confirmed
they actually discussed developing it.

149
00:11:15,900 --> 00:11:18,870
It turns out the victim, Song Min Su,
also came from Chaeum.

150
00:11:19,470 --> 00:11:24,440
As a senior researcher,
he even scored Lee's submission highly.

151
00:11:24,640 --> 00:11:28,480
After he left Chaeum, he and Prof. Han,
Lee Woo Gyeom's doctor,

152
00:11:28,580 --> 00:11:31,080
apparently started
the Jinnam Research Institute.

153
00:11:31,510 --> 00:11:34,450
It's possible he was still in contact
with Lee Woo Gyeom from there.

154
00:11:34,850 --> 00:11:36,650
(Jinnam Medical Research Institute)

155
00:11:51,930 --> 00:11:53,340
(Jinnam Medical Research Institute)

156
00:11:55,470 --> 00:11:57,140
(Final notice:
Unpaid gas bill and service disconnection)

157
00:12:09,850 --> 00:12:12,090
(Jinnam Medical Research Institute)

158
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:17,130
Hey! Stop right there!

159
00:12:17,990 --> 00:12:18,990
Darn it.

160
00:13:07,110 --> 00:13:08,110
Darn it.

161
00:13:22,660 --> 00:13:23,760
Detective Gong.

162
00:13:24,030 --> 00:13:28,530
A man just ran to the Daehan Building lot.
Check the CCTV footage right now.

163
00:13:29,500 --> 00:13:30,500
Right.

164
00:13:35,570 --> 00:13:37,840
Number 5896. Let's go to your cell.

165
00:13:40,710 --> 00:13:43,410
Well, well, if it isn't the good doctor.

166
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:46,050
Hey, I hear you only go after
the worst of the worst.

167
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:48,880
Guess what? I'm a real piece of work.

168
00:13:49,550 --> 00:13:50,990
Come on and kill me too, you jerk.

169
00:13:51,520 --> 00:13:55,960
- I said kill me, you fool!
- What are you looking at? Eyes down!

170
00:13:56,230 --> 00:13:59,960
I'll gouge your eyes out.
I'll see you around. Got it?

171
00:14:01,200 --> 00:14:03,430
You're smiling?
I'll knock your darn teeth out.

172
00:14:03,830 --> 00:14:05,370
Hey! That son of a gun...

173
00:14:14,110 --> 00:14:15,980
(Storage lockers)

174
00:14:33,300 --> 00:14:36,770
Hey, if they're going to lock us up
with a psycho...

175
00:14:37,170 --> 00:14:38,170
For goodness' sake.

176
00:14:38,830 --> 00:14:40,600
How's anyone supposed to feel safe?

177
00:14:48,880 --> 00:14:52,380
- Bae, the kid is here.
- Yes, I'm heading out now, boss.

178
00:14:58,620 --> 00:15:00,790
(Inmate property)

179
00:15:05,690 --> 00:15:06,830
What are you looking at?

180
00:16:12,130 --> 00:16:14,300
You know Hong Jae Gwang, right?
I heard you killed my brother.

181
00:16:14,360 --> 00:16:15,360
You son of a gun.

182
00:16:16,470 --> 00:16:17,530
- Die!
- Die!

183
00:16:17,870 --> 00:16:19,430
Die! You're going to die too!

184
00:16:20,870 --> 00:16:21,870
Die.

185
00:16:25,240 --> 00:16:27,180
You crazy jerk!

186
00:16:32,980 --> 00:16:34,380
Die!

187
00:16:35,020 --> 00:16:37,390
Die! Die!

188
00:16:41,790 --> 00:16:43,730
You idiot! What are you doing, man?

189
00:16:44,160 --> 00:16:45,390
Kill him!

190
00:16:48,460 --> 00:16:49,970
Just die! Die!

191
00:16:53,300 --> 00:16:54,300
What's going on?

192
00:16:58,670 --> 00:16:59,680
You...

193
00:17:02,080 --> 00:17:04,310
You useless piece of shit.

194
00:17:07,250 --> 00:17:08,920
Wait, hold on.

195
00:17:09,650 --> 00:17:11,650
Sorry. I'm sorry. Just wait.

196
00:17:18,030 --> 00:17:22,930
Guards!

197
00:17:26,070 --> 00:17:27,240
Guards!

198
00:17:30,210 --> 00:17:31,740
What's wrong with this guy now?

199
00:17:32,570 --> 00:17:34,440
Hey, are you okay?

200
00:17:42,750 --> 00:17:44,750
- What's happening to him?
- Guards!

201
00:17:45,120 --> 00:17:46,690
Hey! Hey, are you okay?

202
00:17:47,260 --> 00:17:49,060
Hey, snap out of it, you fool!

203
00:18:22,790 --> 00:18:23,790
Professor Han.

204
00:18:25,860 --> 00:18:28,300
Please get me Professor Han Sang Ho.

205
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:37,240
Hello?

206
00:18:38,970 --> 00:18:39,980
Yes.

207
00:18:42,080 --> 00:18:43,080
What?

208
00:18:43,980 --> 00:18:44,980
Okay, I understand.

209
00:18:46,350 --> 00:18:47,350
Mr. Park!

210
00:18:48,080 --> 00:18:50,650
I just heard Lee Woo Gyeom was taken
to the hospital this morning.

211
00:18:56,560 --> 00:19:00,000
They'll most likely reject
the medical demonstration.

212
00:19:06,230 --> 00:19:07,240
Come on, so what?

213
00:19:08,270 --> 00:19:09,970
If I can't do the medical demonstration,

214
00:19:10,210 --> 00:19:11,870
then there's no point
in having this trial.

215
00:19:14,380 --> 00:19:16,080
We need to have a backup plan.

216
00:19:17,050 --> 00:19:19,110
A backup plan? What kind of backup plan?

217
00:19:19,880 --> 00:19:21,850
Is there a better plan
than the medical demonstration?

218
00:19:23,220 --> 00:19:24,220
Lee Woo Gyeom.

219
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:27,590
Let's save a life in here.

220
00:19:28,620 --> 00:19:30,660
Are you out of your mind?

221
00:19:31,330 --> 00:19:34,360
This is a prison. And I'm in solitary.

222
00:19:34,560 --> 00:19:36,570
The trial's over. You're being moved.

223
00:19:44,710 --> 00:19:45,710
Take a good look at this.

224
00:19:46,780 --> 00:19:51,650
These are the inmates' medical records.
Pick a suitable candidate from this list.

225
00:19:52,480 --> 00:19:54,550
I'll take care of the rest.

226
00:19:55,180 --> 00:19:58,320
The only way to make sure
the court can't refuse the medical demo...

227
00:19:59,590 --> 00:20:00,760
is this.

228
00:20:04,260 --> 00:20:06,360
(Central Prison Inmate Medical Records)

229
00:20:06,430 --> 00:20:08,130
(Bae Geun Hyeok)

230
00:20:11,900 --> 00:20:13,000
What are you looking at?

231
00:20:13,100 --> 00:20:16,710
(History: Congenital Corneal Damage)

232
00:20:17,170 --> 00:20:18,810
I get the plan,

233
00:20:19,940 --> 00:20:21,240
but it'll take way too long.

234
00:20:22,510 --> 00:20:24,850
I'm going to improvise a little.

235
00:20:28,850 --> 00:20:29,850
How?

236
00:20:30,120 --> 00:20:31,350
I'll have to put my life on the line.

237
00:20:32,250 --> 00:20:34,020
If I hadn't put my own body
on the line in the first place,

238
00:20:34,420 --> 00:20:37,430
I never would've found the cure.
Besides, you...

239
00:20:38,560 --> 00:20:41,600
- You risked it all for Min Seo?
- You...

240
00:20:42,930 --> 00:20:44,330
You're on trial right now.

241
00:20:45,430 --> 00:20:47,440
- If something goes wrong...
- The worst is a death sentence.

242
00:20:49,100 --> 00:20:50,210
I don't care about that.

243
00:20:51,270 --> 00:20:53,040
As long as I can prove what I am,

244
00:20:55,680 --> 00:20:57,780
the sentence means nothing to me.

245
00:20:59,780 --> 00:21:00,780
Just trust me...

246
00:21:01,880 --> 00:21:02,880
and just watch.

247
00:21:07,760 --> 00:21:09,860
He's showing symptoms
of shock from blood loss.

248
00:21:10,430 --> 00:21:12,830
We've never seen a case this unusual,

249
00:21:13,330 --> 00:21:15,260
so it's a good thing
Professor Han Sang Ho came when he did.

250
00:21:15,830 --> 00:21:18,930
- If we'd treated him rashly, who knows...
- Professor Han Sang Ho?

251
00:21:20,600 --> 00:21:22,070
How would Professor Han Sang Ho
know to come here?

252
00:21:22,200 --> 00:21:25,470
The patient gave us
his contact information.

253
00:21:26,110 --> 00:21:28,410
Said he was a patient of his,
diagnosed with a blood mutation.

254
00:21:32,980 --> 00:21:36,320
Administering it to a human is impossible.

255
00:21:36,820 --> 00:21:39,890
What happened to the man
who was stabbed by Lee Woo Gyeom?

256
00:21:43,460 --> 00:21:47,300
He had severe internal bleeding, was out,
and it was an emergency,

257
00:21:47,800 --> 00:21:50,300
but Lee Woo Gyeom drew his own blood...

258
00:21:50,470 --> 00:21:53,540
and transfused it directly
into the patient, Bae Geun Hyeok.

259
00:21:54,500 --> 00:21:57,240
But get this.
Not only did the stab wound heal,

260
00:21:57,440 --> 00:22:00,040
his congenital corneal damage
was cured as well.

261
00:22:00,340 --> 00:22:02,980
He made a full recovery
in just a few hours.

262
00:22:04,050 --> 00:22:06,450
Is that even possible?

263
00:22:06,650 --> 00:22:09,550
I saw it with my own two eyes,

264
00:22:10,550 --> 00:22:14,390
but I still can't believe it.

265
00:22:17,590 --> 00:22:20,400
(Court)

266
00:22:20,460 --> 00:22:21,460
(Judge Choi Seok Moon)

267
00:22:31,070 --> 00:22:34,440
Regarding the defense's request
for a medical demonstration...

268
00:22:34,880 --> 00:22:36,080
We have reviewed it thoroughly.

269
00:22:37,410 --> 00:22:38,810
And this appellate court,

270
00:22:39,450 --> 00:22:43,080
in agreement with the lower court,
will also deny the medical demonstration.

271
00:22:44,590 --> 00:22:47,590
Therefore, both sides should prepare
for a standard trial.

272
00:22:49,360 --> 00:22:50,890
A wise decision, Your Honor.

273
00:22:52,090 --> 00:22:54,360
We are filing a motion...

274
00:22:56,060 --> 00:22:57,070
for a constitutional review.

275
00:22:57,600 --> 00:23:02,370
- You demand the medical demonstration?
- That's correct.

276
00:23:02,640 --> 00:23:05,010
If Lee Woo Gyeom can truly cure
an incurable disease,

277
00:23:05,840 --> 00:23:09,340
I believe that's ample reason
to consider it in his sentencing.

278
00:23:09,910 --> 00:23:13,080
No.
The court's deliberation on this is over.

279
00:23:19,620 --> 00:23:22,990
Filing a constitutional petition
is at the discretion of the defense,

280
00:23:23,630 --> 00:23:24,730
You may proceed if you must,

281
00:23:25,790 --> 00:23:28,730
but the appeal will proceed as scheduled.
Understood?

282
00:23:29,530 --> 00:23:30,530
Yes, Your Honor.

283
00:23:33,100 --> 00:23:34,140
(Attorney Park, the article is a hit!)

284
00:23:34,200 --> 00:23:35,600
Do you have anything further?

285
00:23:36,040 --> 00:23:38,070
- Nothing further.
- Then we are adjourned.

286
00:23:38,140 --> 00:23:39,140
Your Honor.

287
00:23:42,540 --> 00:23:44,250
Would you please
take a look at this article?

288
00:23:46,080 --> 00:23:49,150
("Serial Killer Lee Woo Gyeom
Saves a Life in Prison!")

289
00:23:55,160 --> 00:23:56,160
One moment.

290
00:23:56,960 --> 00:23:58,630
(Director Oh Hyeon Deuk)

291
00:24:00,100 --> 00:24:01,560
Yes, Mr. Chief Justice.

292
00:24:03,060 --> 00:24:04,900
Yes. I've just seen the article myself,

293
00:24:06,070 --> 00:24:08,070
("Serial Killer Lee Woo Gyeom
Saves a Life in Prison!")

294
00:24:09,070 --> 00:24:11,840
I'll find out what the situation is.

295
00:24:18,110 --> 00:24:20,150
He was cured by a blood transfusion
from Lee Woo Gyeom?

296
00:24:20,580 --> 00:24:23,750
Yes. I just found out
from the article myself,

297
00:24:24,220 --> 00:24:25,890
so I'm looking into the details now.

298
00:24:25,950 --> 00:24:28,460
Seriously, what's with
that jerk Lee Woo Gyeom?

299
00:24:28,960 --> 00:24:31,130
If he had something to prove,
he should've done it way sooner.

300
00:24:31,530 --> 00:24:34,400
He had to know that a death penalty case
goes to a third trial.

301
00:24:35,060 --> 00:24:36,060
Goodness!

302
00:24:36,700 --> 00:24:38,470
What are you going to do now?

303
00:24:39,330 --> 00:24:42,000
Director Oh.
Let's not get ahead of ourselves.

304
00:24:42,240 --> 00:24:43,440
The trial isn't over yet.

305
00:24:44,010 --> 00:24:45,810
- In a situation like this...
- My reputation is on the line,

306
00:24:45,810 --> 00:24:47,380
and I chose to take this case.

307
00:24:48,110 --> 00:24:52,480
- Please, don't doubt me.
- What? Hey, do you even hear yourself?

308
00:24:55,950 --> 00:24:56,990
This court,

309
00:24:57,250 --> 00:24:59,590
after carefully reviewing
the defendant Lee Woo Gyeom's...

310
00:24:59,990 --> 00:25:03,760
recent act of providing
medical treatment in prison,

311
00:25:04,190 --> 00:25:08,560
has determined that it is necessary
to verify his medical abilities.

312
00:25:08,760 --> 00:25:12,170
An unprecedented decision has been made
in South Korea's constitutional history.

313
00:25:12,470 --> 00:25:16,840
The court handling the Lee Woo Gyeom case
has approved the medical demonstration.

314
00:25:20,140 --> 00:25:21,240
How did this happen?

315
00:25:21,780 --> 00:25:24,010
Someone named Professor Han Sang Ho
came to the hospital...

316
00:25:24,280 --> 00:25:25,280
Professor Han Sang Ho?

317
00:25:25,650 --> 00:25:29,220
According to the attending physician,
Lee Woo Gyeom called Prof. Han Sang Ho,

318
00:25:29,280 --> 00:25:31,750
and he confirmed that Bae Geun Hyeok
was transfused with Lee Woo Gyeom's blood.

319
00:25:32,020 --> 00:25:33,890
What about the files I requested
from Detective Gong?

320
00:25:34,020 --> 00:25:35,020
I left them over there.

321
00:25:35,420 --> 00:25:38,090
I checked Lee Woo Gyeom's visitor log
and the surrounding CCTV footage...

322
00:25:38,160 --> 00:25:39,730
and filtered out anyone
who seemed suspicious.

323
00:25:46,630 --> 00:25:48,700
(Han Sang Ho, Medical Professional)

324
00:25:48,770 --> 00:25:51,570
(Han Sang Ho, Medical Professional)

325
00:25:59,050 --> 00:26:00,180
(Jinnam Medical Research Institute)

326
00:26:08,560 --> 00:26:10,190
(Chief Pyo Kang Won)

327
00:26:25,410 --> 00:26:26,710
Hello, Prosecutor Cha.

328
00:26:28,210 --> 00:26:29,210
Prosecutor.

329
00:26:29,740 --> 00:26:30,880
How have you been?

330
00:26:33,520 --> 00:26:34,520
The thing is...

331
00:26:35,250 --> 00:26:37,120
I came across some information,

332
00:26:37,650 --> 00:26:39,450
and I was about to leak it to the press,

333
00:26:40,390 --> 00:26:42,620
but I was afraid of
the earful you'd give me.

334
00:26:44,160 --> 00:26:45,630
I'm a little busy.

335
00:26:46,290 --> 00:26:47,660
Just get to the point.

336
00:26:48,930 --> 00:26:49,930
You really...

337
00:26:51,070 --> 00:26:52,330
never change, do you?

338
00:26:53,700 --> 00:26:55,670
What is it you have for me?

339
00:26:58,540 --> 00:26:59,970
Attorney Park's daughter...

340
00:27:01,180 --> 00:27:02,640
is terminally ill.

341
00:27:05,080 --> 00:27:08,280
His wife is a doctor,
so instead of taking her elsewhere,

342
00:27:09,120 --> 00:27:12,950
she's apparently treating their daughter
at the hospital where she works.

343
00:27:13,820 --> 00:27:16,220
I'd bet that's why he took
Lee Woo Gyeom's case, don't you think?

344
00:27:19,690 --> 00:27:22,930
I'm not really interested
in people's family drama.

345
00:27:23,770 --> 00:27:26,830
How about another fun fact, then?

346
00:27:27,240 --> 00:27:29,240
(The Prosecution)

347
00:27:32,170 --> 00:27:33,580
(Medical Demonstration Applicant List)

348
00:27:33,640 --> 00:27:35,040
(Selected Institution:
Chaeum Medical Center)

349
00:27:35,110 --> 00:27:36,210
(Batten Disease,
Park Min Seo, Female, Age 9)

350
00:27:36,280 --> 00:27:37,510
(Park Han Jun, Hong Jae Hee)

351
00:27:40,420 --> 00:27:41,550
So you didn't know.

352
00:27:44,550 --> 00:27:47,620
Then I take it you know Professor Han.

353
00:27:48,660 --> 00:27:49,920
Professor Han?

354
00:27:51,060 --> 00:27:53,360
When Lee Woo Gyeom was in a coma...

355
00:27:54,060 --> 00:27:58,930
Did you also know Professor Han
used him as a test subject?

356
00:28:04,040 --> 00:28:07,440
- What's your source?
- The source isn't important.

357
00:28:08,410 --> 00:28:10,180
What matters is that before you knew,

358
00:28:10,510 --> 00:28:13,010
someone had already
finished their business...

359
00:28:13,080 --> 00:28:15,750
concerning Lee Woo Gyeom.

360
00:28:16,120 --> 00:28:17,520
What are you implying?

361
00:28:17,920 --> 00:28:19,650
It means if you dig too deep,

362
00:28:20,460 --> 00:28:23,630
you could get hurt, Prosecutor.

363
00:28:30,570 --> 00:28:33,800
His phone is turned completely off.
And he's our key witness.

364
00:28:40,040 --> 00:28:41,740
You think he knew we'd be back?

365
00:28:55,020 --> 00:28:56,120
Maybe it's not us.

366
00:28:57,360 --> 00:28:59,460
He could be avoiding someone else.

367
00:29:04,830 --> 00:29:05,870
Thanks for all your hard work.

368
00:29:06,300 --> 00:29:08,900
So now, I just have to do well
in the medical demonstration.

369
00:29:09,900 --> 00:29:11,110
Let me confirm something first.

370
00:29:12,070 --> 00:29:13,070
About what?

371
00:29:14,640 --> 00:29:16,110
What was Professor Han's part in this?

372
00:29:16,810 --> 00:29:17,850
Professor Han?

373
00:29:20,450 --> 00:29:21,780
I reached out to him myself.

374
00:29:23,790 --> 00:29:26,320
- What's your relationship with him?
- What do you mean, relationship?

375
00:29:26,820 --> 00:29:28,160
He was just my doctor.

376
00:29:29,260 --> 00:29:31,960
If Professor Han knew about
your condition from the start,

377
00:29:33,430 --> 00:29:34,560
then he must have known about the cure...

378
00:29:35,360 --> 00:29:36,560
as well.

379
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:38,470
What are you talking about?
He didn't know.

380
00:29:39,570 --> 00:29:44,270
And stop trying to connect the two of us.
He and I are nothing alike.

381
00:29:45,440 --> 00:29:46,440
How so?

382
00:29:47,510 --> 00:29:51,410
I'm telling you. That man has no idea
how to make the cure.

383
00:29:53,050 --> 00:29:54,950
He spent his whole life
trying to develop a cure,

384
00:29:55,020 --> 00:29:58,450
but he failed. Of course
I'm different from a loser like him.

385
00:29:59,590 --> 00:30:03,590
He visited me before and kept asking
how I developed the cure.

386
00:30:04,090 --> 00:30:06,160
It was so annoying.

387
00:30:07,200 --> 00:30:10,030
Still, I guess I can see why
someone like him would do that.

388
00:30:11,130 --> 00:30:14,140
- Is that all?
- What'd you expect? That we were dating?

389
00:30:18,110 --> 00:30:21,510
Do you happen to know where
Professor Han might be staying?

390
00:30:23,180 --> 00:30:24,450
Why? Can't you reach him?

391
00:30:24,710 --> 00:30:27,120
No, I can't get ahold of him.
For our case,

392
00:30:27,720 --> 00:30:30,350
he's the only witness
who can testify about you.

393
00:30:31,950 --> 00:30:34,120
Let's not worry about Professor Han...

394
00:30:34,920 --> 00:30:36,620
and just focus on
the medical demonstration.

395
00:30:37,590 --> 00:30:39,090
We're so close to the finish line.

396
00:30:39,660 --> 00:30:41,130
We need to see this demonstration
through to the end.

397
00:30:41,530 --> 00:30:45,100
Instead of looking for Professor Han,
go buy a gift for Min Seo.

398
00:31:06,820 --> 00:31:09,490
You pulled off the medical demonstration
after all.

399
00:31:10,560 --> 00:31:11,590
Congratulations.

400
00:31:14,260 --> 00:31:15,630
You know, it's amazing...

401
00:31:16,330 --> 00:31:17,430
how you never change.

402
00:31:19,130 --> 00:31:21,000
Then and now, whenever you lie,

403
00:31:21,700 --> 00:31:23,700
the corner of your mouth
curls up slightly.

404
00:31:24,570 --> 00:31:25,710
When do I do that?

405
00:31:26,370 --> 00:31:29,540
And when you're embarrassed,
you always look away.

406
00:31:30,140 --> 00:31:31,180
Some things never change.

407
00:31:32,980 --> 00:31:35,950
Why on earth do you have to go through
with this medical demonstration?

408
00:31:37,120 --> 00:31:38,190
To prove his motive.

409
00:31:38,750 --> 00:31:39,950
But he already confessed.

410
00:31:40,690 --> 00:31:44,160
If his confession were enough,
then his sentence should be reconsidered.

411
00:31:45,430 --> 00:31:46,860
Is that really why you're doing this?

412
00:31:47,730 --> 00:31:49,530
Just to get his sentence reduced?

413
00:31:49,830 --> 00:31:51,300
Why? Does that make you nervous?

414
00:31:52,000 --> 00:31:54,370
You're the one who's nervous, not me.

415
00:31:55,540 --> 00:31:57,510
Why did you hide
what's happening with Min Seo?

416
00:31:57,970 --> 00:32:01,280
Hiding something
and not saying anything are different.

417
00:32:01,780 --> 00:32:02,780
Besides,

418
00:32:03,110 --> 00:32:05,880
why would you need to know about
the opposing counsel's personal life?

419
00:32:08,450 --> 00:32:09,450
Stay out of it.

420
00:32:10,380 --> 00:32:12,050
So is that why,
back at the training institute,

421
00:32:13,220 --> 00:32:16,860
you'd get drunk and keep telling me
that, "People come before the law,"

422
00:32:16,920 --> 00:32:18,460
and stay up all night repeating yourself?

423
00:32:20,090 --> 00:32:21,100
Han Jun.

424
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:23,500
Even now, at the Judicial Research
and Training Institute,

425
00:32:24,030 --> 00:32:26,100
you're still held up as a model example.

426
00:32:28,300 --> 00:32:29,470
Well, I guess it's about time...

427
00:32:30,040 --> 00:32:31,340
for that to change, then.

428
00:32:31,410 --> 00:32:35,280
What happened to the prosecutor who always
put away every scumbag he could find?

429
00:32:35,340 --> 00:32:38,150
I'm simply doing the best I can
for my client.

430
00:32:38,210 --> 00:32:39,880
But this is Lee Woo Gyeom
we're talking about.

431
00:32:41,120 --> 00:32:43,180
You're really going to accept help
from a murderer like him?

432
00:32:43,750 --> 00:32:46,690
Since when have you ever cared
who the defendant is?

433
00:32:47,490 --> 00:32:50,160
You just need a high-profile case
to make a name for yourself.

434
00:32:51,330 --> 00:32:52,530
And what's wrong with that?

435
00:32:52,530 --> 00:32:54,200
Don't use Lee Woo Gyeom's
death sentence...

436
00:32:55,860 --> 00:32:58,300
as a stepping stone for your career.

437
00:32:59,200 --> 00:33:02,370
You can reach your goals
without Lee Woo Gyeom, but I...

438
00:33:03,800 --> 00:33:05,710
I need him right now.

439
00:33:06,610 --> 00:33:10,240
You think Lee Woo Gyeom
is really going to cure Min Seo?

440
00:33:10,750 --> 00:33:12,180
What if he's lying?

441
00:33:12,710 --> 00:33:14,780
There's no guarantee
the treatment will even work.

442
00:33:15,980 --> 00:33:19,020
That's why I'm saying we should find
a legitimate way to do this.

443
00:33:19,720 --> 00:33:21,620
I'll help in any way I can.

444
00:33:21,990 --> 00:33:25,290
If you need money for the treatment...
I know you won't like this, but...

445
00:33:25,360 --> 00:33:26,360
Yi Yeon.

446
00:33:30,700 --> 00:33:31,900
That's enough.

447
00:33:36,440 --> 00:33:37,610
I'll see you in court.

448
00:33:38,040 --> 00:33:40,610
You know this is wrong.

449
00:33:41,240 --> 00:33:43,610
Why are you giving
a guy like that a chance?

450
00:33:44,780 --> 00:33:48,020
- Let me help you get the treatment.
- That's not what this is about, darn it!

451
00:33:49,480 --> 00:33:50,990
If it was something
a treatment could solve,

452
00:33:51,650 --> 00:33:53,020
I wouldn't have gone this far.

453
00:33:54,190 --> 00:33:55,990
I look at that jerk, Lee Woo Gyeom,

454
00:33:57,390 --> 00:33:59,230
and I second-guess myself
hundreds of times a day.

455
00:34:00,290 --> 00:34:02,930
I told myself I'd rather die
than defend that monster.

456
00:34:05,070 --> 00:34:06,630
But then... My daughter, Min Seo...

457
00:34:08,300 --> 00:34:09,740
is really dying.

458
00:34:11,410 --> 00:34:13,870
They said she could die any second,
not tomorrow, but right now.

459
00:34:15,510 --> 00:34:17,180
That was a wake-up call for me.

460
00:34:18,610 --> 00:34:20,750
I realized what I've been living
for all this time.

461
00:34:23,850 --> 00:34:24,850
I...

462
00:34:25,990 --> 00:34:27,990
don't care about anything else
in this world...

463
00:34:28,760 --> 00:34:30,320
except for getting my Min Seo treated.

464
00:34:31,290 --> 00:34:32,830
Even if this is the wrong choice,

465
00:34:33,960 --> 00:34:35,900
I would make it all over again.

466
00:34:37,300 --> 00:34:38,300
Understand?

467
00:34:42,800 --> 00:34:43,800
Han Jun...

468
00:34:52,150 --> 00:34:53,150
Yi Yeon.

469
00:34:55,950 --> 00:34:58,090
Then all you have to do
is beat me in court.

470
00:35:07,960 --> 00:35:08,960
To be honest,

471
00:35:12,300 --> 00:35:14,340
I'd rather you win.

472
00:35:34,060 --> 00:35:36,060
(Woori Iseul)

473
00:35:59,810 --> 00:36:01,850
(Lee Chang Se, 50,
Terminal Cancer, Receiving Treatment)

474
00:36:01,920 --> 00:36:03,980
(Additional Evidence Needed,
Moon Se Guk's Treatment)

475
00:36:14,100 --> 00:36:15,130
Jae Hee.

476
00:36:16,200 --> 00:36:20,030
They'll announce the recipients soon.
So let's just wait a little longer.

477
00:36:34,880 --> 00:36:35,880
Mr. Jo.

478
00:36:36,350 --> 00:36:38,750
- Hey. Thank you.
- Careful, it's hot.

479
00:36:40,120 --> 00:36:42,290
Now all that's left is selecting
the participant for the demonstration.

480
00:36:43,560 --> 00:36:45,090
You think the attorney's going to be okay?

481
00:36:45,990 --> 00:36:49,560
He must have mixed feelings.
He's probably getting his hopes up.

482
00:36:50,460 --> 00:36:51,470
Goodness.

483
00:36:52,900 --> 00:36:54,700
It still doesn't feel real to me.

484
00:36:55,140 --> 00:36:56,140
What doesn't?

485
00:36:56,400 --> 00:36:58,270
That an incurable disease
can actually be cured.

486
00:37:00,940 --> 00:37:03,680
It's not just you.
The whole world feels that way.

487
00:37:04,250 --> 00:37:08,420
Inventions and discoveries have never been
welcomed with open arms in human history.

488
00:37:08,980 --> 00:37:11,050
The Earth's rotation and revolution,

489
00:37:11,320 --> 00:37:15,520
the law of universal gravitation,
the discovery of the New World...

490
00:37:17,120 --> 00:37:20,530
Do you think people will come
to accept this over time?

491
00:37:21,300 --> 00:37:22,330
I wonder.

492
00:37:22,860 --> 00:37:23,860
I hope so.

493
00:37:25,970 --> 00:37:26,970
No.

494
00:37:29,270 --> 00:37:30,270
They have to.

495
00:37:36,210 --> 00:37:38,880
We're hearing that the patient
for the demo will be selected today.

496
00:37:39,080 --> 00:37:43,450
Reports say Lee Woo Gyeom's lawyer's child
is a top choice.

497
00:37:44,020 --> 00:37:47,220
That choice makes sense, and it's likely
why he took the case in the first place.

498
00:37:47,660 --> 00:37:51,230
Right. Being first brings pressure
and the risks involved.

499
00:37:56,660 --> 00:37:58,070
(Quiet)

500
00:37:58,130 --> 00:37:59,870
(Medical Demonstration
Participant Selection Meeting in Progress)

501
00:38:04,040 --> 00:38:05,040
Your Honor.

502
00:38:05,740 --> 00:38:07,580
Regarding the selection...

503
